[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   Step 146: SCLK radial lapse-gradient and bipolar-sign channel (step_b110).
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   Step 141 tested signed level *steps* at the four crossings.  A second
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   observable in the same one-way record is the drift's spatial
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   structure: the signed fractional oscillator offset dnu versus
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   heliocentric radius and versus the craft's direction on the bipolar
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   axis.  The two Voyagers exited toward opposite polarities of the
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   measured bipolar field -- Voyager 1 north of the ecliptic toward the
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   antapex-side lobe, Voyager 2 south toward the apex side.  A bipolar
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   lapse field predicts opposite-signed outer-region drift between them;
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   ordinary oscillator ageing predicts same-signed, time-organized drift.
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   T1  Signed drift vs radius: Spearman dnu vs r_au per craft over the
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   full record and the outer region (r > 60 AU), with the NH1
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   control (whose dnu is kernel-frozen, registered as such).
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   T2  Bipolar-sign test: outer-region (r > 60 AU) per-year drift slope
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   for V1 vs V2 -- opposite sign predicted by the bipolar geometry --
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   together with each craft's median outer asymptote direction and
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   its separation from the declared axis, anti-axis and CMB axis.
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   T3  Radius-vs-ageing discrimination: per-AU and per-year drift
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   coefficients for the two Voyagers, and the partial correlation
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   dnu ~ r_au | mission-age.  Radius and age are ~99.9 per cent
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   collinear outbound, so the registered discriminator is the
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   outer-region sign split (T2), not the full-record correlation.
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   T4  Directional coupling: each craft's post-60 AU drift slope
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   against the cosine of its trajectory direction to the bipolar
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   (CMB) axis -- the signed quantity a bipolar lapse gradient
[2026-09-20 12:25:49 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 146]   predicts to reverse between the two asymptotes.
